            "review_title": "Review at Blue Sky Restaurant/ Elios Hotel",
            "review_text": "Salantha R\nPaarl, South Africa6 contributions\n0\nVery noisy surroundings, with rather small rooms.\nMar 2018 • Couples\nWe had 3 nights at Elios Hotel as part of the Halong tour package. Initial room was called Senior room with window. That's apparently above a superior but below a deluxe.\nVery small room with an even smaller window. Also old and outdated but clean. We landed at 11pm with music/noise blaring from loudspeakers from the park below. At 2am, I sent an email to Tracy from Halong Tours asking for our hotel to be changed. Sleep finally at 3am, as tour began at 8am. On return from tour, we received an upgraded room, a more spacious deluxe room with a more dated bathroom. Same loud music but could barely hear it as we now faced the opposite side of the park. The Sky Bar on the 12th floor served breakfast. A very good variety of both eastern and western food. Very busy hotel and breakfast but worth the views and selection of breakfast. However not a hotel I would stay in again as just too busy and noisy, with limited space in an already crazy busy city.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 18, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
