            "review_title": "Review at Blue Sky Restaurant/ Elios Hotel",
            "review_text": "MOCCalifornia\nSan Jose, California97 contributions\n0\nLovely rooftop spot - Alfredo spaghetti to die for\nDec 2017 • Solo\nI was booked at the Elios Hotel for 18 days in December 2017 so I frequently ate in the rooftop restaurant. The Alfredo spaghetti was to die for - you don't need to add the grated cheese they provide since it is already so rich and creamy. The fried rice and Thai chicken was also excellent and like all their main dishes, plentiful. After several days of stuffing myself with the pasta, I tried their Russian and then their tuna salads. Both wonderful. You don't need to order anything else when you order the Russian salad - it is a full course. They have a nice selection of beer and the brandy was fine. My only complaint was the lack of any dessert. They have caramel custard on the menu. After asking for it three separate times, I finally said, \"You don't have it, do you.\" The waiter replied, \"No, it has eggs and it is hard for the cook.\" Made no sense to me. I suggested they at least get some ice cream as the Australian family next to me had several kids who all wanted ice cream. And nearly all the Westerners asked about dessert on the occasions I was present. Since a bakery is almost next door, I can't figure out why they just don't buy some treats there and resell them for desserts. They are losing money because of their failure to serve dessert. \nOf course the rooftop is a lovely place to eat.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 18, 2018",
